# RX-02 native failure qualification and error preservation
PR: https://github.com/applicate2628/mcp-local-hub/pull/625
Commit:
7ce04f7ef2f96680ed94db1edaf77cf0358421c4
Base: 8698d24e622253b8d9e2d1bd96d29fb97e5de4f1

## Actual implementation
One narrow library change: unexpected native attribute-size-query failure returns original io::Error, preserving raw_os_error; impossible success/empty buffer shapes remain explicit internal errors.
Private actual invalid-count repro returned OS87 but old wrapper lost code. Public callers normally select1/2 attributes: no claim that u32MAX is a public supported input.
Test-only module uses real reduced-right handles/private-slot substitution, suspend count changes and native protect-from-close. No public injection feature, global hooks, new runtime layer or dependencies.

## Fresh evidence
Nine native-failure tests: attribute query; repeated missing image; resume denied; unexpected suspend count; wait denied; exit-code query denied; Job-query denied; failed-stop replay prevention; seven subsets of protected close failure.
Negative controls WAIT_FAILED->timeout and cleanup->Complete were detected. Original source restored before final suite.
Full crate:39 native integration tests,12 unit tests(9native-failure+3encoding),2compile-fail docs. Three full debug runs and one release run passed with zero ignored/filtered.
Clippy(all-targets,-Dwarnings),fmt,git diff-check passed. Runtime/public API/Cargo manifest and lock otherwise unchanged.
Windows11 build26100/x86_64/Rust1.99.1 offline locked cached dependencies; no target installation or Unix runtime/cross-build in this increment.
Only own bounded hidden fixture/test binaries run. Protector removes its own flag only from confirmed live handle; count after fixture cleanup returns. No product rule to retry ambiguous close.

## Review and limits
Self-review across requirements, correctness, ownership, security, compatibility and complexity;13 relevant skills applied and primary API sources checked. No independent agent/reviewer run.
Not complete failure coverage: allocator/Job setup/attribute init+update/in-progress create and already blocked IO remain. Calling-side noninheritable conversion, Go/Rust interface, native Unix, performance comparison and production admission remain.
The failed stop result and later known execution settlement are separate; no automatic retry. Repeated finish returns stored cleanup failure, not proof of every possible kernel call count.
Previously reported first-call handle delta remains unresolved; warm repeated-create evidence does not establish zero first-call growth.

## Recovery / preservation
Exact remote head matches checked local head and tested source hashes; working clone clean. Needed source/evidence/cache retained outside trash inside D:\dev\ChatGPT.
No newly discarded on-disk mutation backup was created; mutations were restored from in-memory exact bytes. Unique failed/success evidence preserved. No trash emptying.
Other code PRs, active main workspace, installed Hub/config/autostart/secrets untouched. No merge/release/install/paid-model/provider or explicit bot/CI dispatch.
Next integration boundary: Go↔Rust, preserving one resource owner and the now-tested outcomes; this task does not assert its implementation.
===== END RESULTS.md =====

